{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Smart Data Validation", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about smart data validation.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Reads and Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. Exchanges simple information on the data validation and data warehouses.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Zero Conditional in Negative", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We use the&nbsp;<b>zero conditional</b>&nbsp;to express a result that will always happen.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The&nbsp;<b>zero conditional</b>&nbsp;structure consists of two clauses in present simple, one with the conditional particle <b><i>if</i></b> or <b><i>when</i></b> and the main clause.<i><br /> <br /> </i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Use the following structure to make a sentence using the first conditional form:</p> <ol style=\"text-align: justify;\"> <li><b>Idea 1 (present simple) + if + idea 2 (present simple)</b></li> <li><b>If + idea 2 (present simple) + , + idea 1 (present simple)</b></li> </ol> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i><br /> </i>Examples:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><i><b>&nbsp;1.&nbsp;</b>Projects <b>work</b>&nbsp;well <b>if</b> you&nbsp;<b>understand&nbsp;</b>the basic concepts of information.<br /></i><b><i>2. If&nbsp;</i></b><i>you&nbsp;<b>understand&nbsp;</b>the basic concepts of information<b>,&nbsp;</b>projects&nbsp;<b>work</b>&nbsp;well.</i></p> <p><i> <b>1. If&nbsp;</b>you&nbsp;<b>compare&nbsp;</b>the information<b>,</b>&nbsp;it&nbsp;<b>matches</b>.<br /></i><i><b>2.</b> The information&nbsp;<b>matches&nbsp;</b><b>if&nbsp;</b>you&nbsp;<b>compare</b>&nbsp;it.</i></p> <p><i><br /> </i>In order to make negative sentences suing the first conditional form, we add the negative particle &ldquo;<b><i>not</i></b>&rdquo; in the <b><i>if clause</i></b>. In this case, the existence of such a negative situation propitiates a special fact.<i>&nbsp;<br /> <br /> </i>Examples:<i>&nbsp;<br /> <b>1. If</b>&nbsp;you&nbsp;<b>don't organize</b>&nbsp;the information, the database&nbsp;<b>becomes</b>&nbsp;a mess.&nbsp;<br /></i><i>2. The database&nbsp;<b>becomes</b>&nbsp;a mess <b>if</b>&nbsp;you&nbsp;<b>don't organize</b>&nbsp;the information.</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If companies don't define the data properly, it obstructs our work from the beginning. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you don't do it, your database becomes ineffective, possibly because there can be duplicate information.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Countable and Uncountable Nouns to Talk about Data Validation", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There are some specific nouns that we use when we talk about smart data validation; some of them are countable and some others are not.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Remember that we divide nouns into countable and uncountable nouns.</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br /> Examples:</p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br /> <i>I have <b>two computers&nbsp;</b>(&ldquo;Computer&rdquo; is a countable noun).</i>&nbsp;<br /> <i>I have&nbsp;<b>some information</b></i>&nbsp;(&ldquo;Information&rdquo; is uncountable; you can't determine it by numbers).&nbsp;<br /> <br /> When we talk about smart data validation, we often use the following countable and uncountable nouns:&nbsp;<br /> </p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Countable Nouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Uncountable Nouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Storage\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Volume\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Database\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Data\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Program\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Software\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Owner\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ownership\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "So, as I was saying, we have three basic concepts: definition, ownership, and stewardship. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We can understand that smart data validation comprises the delimitation of the database and the definition of the processing environment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Data ownership concerns the people who make decisions that affect data.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Misplaced and Dangling Modifiers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Misplaced and dangling modifiers</strong>&nbsp;are words, phrases, or clauses that are in the wrong place modifying the wrong noun.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In English, we have a special way of organizing the words or phrases that we use to determine or describe things and people. If we fail in the correct organization, we could determine or describe the wrong element of the sentence.<br /> <br /> Example:&nbsp;<br /> <i>The&nbsp;<b>wrong</b>&nbsp;amount of data</i>&nbsp;(The word &ldquo;wrong&rdquo; determines the noun &ldquo;amount&rdquo;)&nbsp;<br /> <i>The amount of&nbsp;<b>wrong&nbsp;</b>data&nbsp;</i>(The word &ldquo;wrong&rdquo; determines the noun &ldquo;data&rdquo;)&nbsp;<br /> <br /> As you can see in the examples above, there is a difference in meaning between the two sentences. The difference is not so notorious in that case because the sentences are out of a context, but in smart data validation context, the determined data would vary between the two sentences.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> Let's use a more basic example:&nbsp;<br /> <br /> <i>Jack drinks a&nbsp;<b>hot</b>&nbsp;cup of tea</i>.&nbsp;<br /> In this sentence, the adjective &ldquo;hot&rdquo; is describing the cup and not the beverage, which makes this a weird sentence.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> <i>Jack drinks a cup of&nbsp;<b>hot</b>&nbsp;tea.</i>&nbsp;<br /> In this new sentence, the adjective &ldquo;hot&rdquo; is just behind the word &ldquo;tea&rdquo; and makes the sentence clear by determining the temperature of the beverage instead of the temperature of the container.</p>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "obstruct ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to interrupt the progress of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If companies don't define the data properly, it obstructs our work from the beginning. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "metric-gathering functionality ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "function in which metrics for specific data are brought together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: At this stage, we use data-modeling techniques and set metric-gathering functionality for the different operational processes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "concern ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to relate to or be connected to", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On the other hand, data ownership concerns the people who make decisions that affect data, such as defining data (data definition) and considering its validity level. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "duplicate information ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "information that appears more than once in a database", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you don't do it, your database becomes ineffective, possibly because there can be duplicate information. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "delimitation ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "definition of limits or edges", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can understand that smart data validation comprises the delimitation of the database ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "validity ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the quality of being valid according to specific terms", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On the other hand, data ownership concerns the people who make decisions that affect data, such as defining data (data definition) and considering its validity level. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le03ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "On the web, look for information about the most common forms of data validation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a poster showing the most relevant ones.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Show it to your classmates.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I search for further information about data validation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I organize information about data validation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present information to partners.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can read and write about smart data validation.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write a short paragraph to describe various forms of smart data validation.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can understand information related to smart data validation.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "How important is setting an appropriate data validation process for an organization?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "How would you avoid issues during the data validation processes?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "How can we 